  "packageHash": "nQJKxx6HsIMT8B0QyYqC2tqMZe67w7T+2Q1XlOmoMmSPZ+SHpuDe+SI8B2cI+RhEmGlQXLMUb04XK9tkISk5og==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 278158,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/Cynicszm/FlatFiles",
  "published": "2026-09-25T13:05:43.227Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "A record read through a type mapper no longer copies the parsed values out of the reader, the reader fills one array of parsed values for the whole read rather than a new one for every record, and a type mapper now parses each value into the member that holds it rather than boxing it on the way. Define<T> has also lost its new() constraint: a type with no parameterless constructor is built by handing its constructor the parsed values, matched to its parameters by name, which maps a positional record, a type whose properties are get-only, and a type that validates what it is given. Measured on 10,000 records of 13 columns, a delimited read allocated 741 bytes a record and now allocates 613, a fixed-length read 1,157 and now 1,029, and the same reads through a type mapper 879 and 388, 1,295 and 732. No breaking changes.",
